with more than 15 million players online  Call of Duty warzone made a huge impact  in its opening week so whether you're  brand new to the game or have played  since launch we've got you covered with  eight more tips that you might not know  we all know that the opening minutes of  any battle royale are stressful to speed  up the looting process set your looting  style to contextual press by going to  menu controller use and reload behavior  then switch it to contextual tap this  makes it so you can simply tap the  looting button rather than holding in  town be careful though this one changes  the way you reload as well with a map as  large as a bar dance long-range scopes  in your loadout are always a good idea  the only problem is the glint of your  lens can easily give away your position  in post launch updates even night vision  and thermal sights were giving glint to  get around this pick a merc thermal  optic losing your super long-range isn't  so bad with the added benefit of thermal  detection it's perfect for checking out  what lies ahead by now you've probably  been targeted for a bounty avoiding the  price on your head by evasion and  running up the clock can make you some  money but if you're brave enough so can  fighting back keep an eye out for the  threat indicator and you can plan an  ambush or a counter-attack with your  squad holding out in a taller building  can help weed out any enemy squads  nearby of course now write hunt for them  is always a welcomed option  to get to your LZ as quickly as you can  cut your parachute and tilt your player  down nose first to your desired location  as you near ground level quickly open  and cut your parachute again before  touching down you should also be  checking your surroundings by tapping  the shoulder button to fly with a  third-person view  keep in mind that the fall distance here  is a little more forgiving than you  think you can safely fall without a  parachute roughly two stories also for  your adrenaline junkies out there once  you've cut your parachute you're free to  equip your gun and fire at other flying  targets just don't get distracted and  fall to your death driving around in any  vehicle makes a ton of noise and even  makes you visible on the radar here's an  old battlefield trick you may remember  swapping your seat can help you dodge  oncoming fire switching seats with your  squad mate can easily throw up anyone  who's firing at you while it's not  always a sure thing it's an easy way to  save some precious HP before you run  their asses over and if you're in a  helicopter you can use this technique  for a better position to sharp shoot at  enemies below if you've made it to the  Gulag with a friend you can help each  other out in a few ways while the  pinging system is disabled players with  mics can eat each other using call-outs  during the 1 v1 battle  spray-painting your squad mate a bright  color can also distinguish who's who  down in the pit also while watching from  above you can set off explosives like c4  and claymores with rocks previously we  talked about how taking on contracts can  help your team make some fast cash but  if you want to make some serious dough  try taking them on back-to-back  contracts have a continual bonus the  more you complete the higher the bonus  completing 5 contracts can score you  tons of XP thousands in cash and a shot  at some legendary loot other ways to  earn some serious cash include wiping  out entire enemy squads avoiding those  bounties and of course looking out for  those orange supply crates now for some  door etiquette if you've been playing  warzone without having played modern  warfare know that you don't need to  always hold down the button to get  through a door simply sprinting into it  will get the job done but be careful  it's extremely loud  you can also quietly see what's on the  other side of the door by aiming down  your sights and slowly approaching it  for a useful peak option and just in  case you didn't know double tapping the  Run button lets you super sprint for a  second if you have some tips that didn't  make the list share them in the comments  below and if you're interested in more  war zone tips feel free to watch our  other video with nine essential tips on  how to help you win for continued  coverage of call of duty war zone keep  it here at GameSpot  [Music]  you
 

